abstract: >-
  TapeLM (variant A) couples a frozen dual-channel character-curve encoder with
  zero-training fingerprint modules—lexicon calibration, episodic slots, subject writes,
  and hop/bind composition—in the same normalized fp-space as next-token generation.
  The artifact documents matched-GPT parity, zero-train fp capabilities (calibration, recall, edit,
  stream, hops), honest fair GPT+RAG comparisons, capability wins on noisy/OOV text and slot unlearn,
  and explicit limits (generative fingerprints, hybrid rerankers, internalization Stages 210–212).
